    "identifier": "MTG-70",
    "title": "Prove ContentPack sharing and clone allocation boundary",
    "description": "Prove Runtime State Foundation KR1 without restoring the withdrawn W2-179 performance claims. Add focused executable Rust coverage showing that independently created environments for the same admitted content version and every exact search/root/sibling clone retain the same immutable Arc<ContentPack> identity/content digest, while mutable MatchState facts remain branch-isolated. Add deterministic allocation measurements that distinguish Arc/reference bookkeeping and mutable-state cloning from immutable ContentPack/CardDefinition storage, including a pack-size variation or equivalent controlled check proving clone allocations do not scale with immutable definition bytes. Record the measurement method, workload, build profile, source revision, hardware, raw counts/bytes, and failure threshold in a checked artifact or test output. Preserve Python and fixed-action ABIs. Do not implement undo/page-COW, select a branching design, duplicate W2-197/W2-207, or claim general step/rollout performance. All Python commands must use uv; rebuild the PyO3 extension after Rust changes. Once W2-196 has landed, rebase immediately before headless lf pr land -c; never use lf pr submit.",
